/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Johnson.MetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 66`, `matAt x 57` and `(x 75, x 76)` are a weak fit of `Johnson.MetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem johnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Johnson.MetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.polyhedron Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.S N 66 57 75 := by
  rw [Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.len_eq Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.sqrt_spec (by decide +kernel)) Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.par_ok Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.zs_eq Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.weak_ok Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.poly_eq Pose.JohnsonMetabiaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.ok

